---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DetailA from '../components/DetailA.astro';
import ContactBlock from '../components/ContactBlock.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Method" description="How a Statecraft Systems build runs: one conversation, working versions reviewed in rounds, a written handover at launch, then you or we run it.">
  <section class="wrap page-head">
    <h1>How a build runs.</h1>
    <p class="lede">A build starts with a conversation with the person who does the work now. After that it goes in rounds. Each round you get a working version at a private address, open it on your phone and leave comments on the page. At launch we write down how everything works, and you either run it yourself or have Statecraft Systems run it on a monthly plan. A small site takes one to three weeks.</p>
  </section>

  <DetailA heading="Four steps. The second one repeats." />

  <section class="wrap split">
    <div class="left">
      <h2>In more detail.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="right prose">
      <h2>A working version first</h2>
      <p>We do not send a proposal or a mock-up. The first thing you get is a working version, usually a rough one, because it is easier to say what is wrong with something you can use.</p>
      <h2>Review on the page</h2>
      <p>Each version has a private address that opens on your phone. You tap the thing you want changed and write a note, and the note reaches us attached to that part of the page.</p>
      <p>When we need a decision from you, we send a question with answers to tap. The next version includes your answers and a list of what changed.</p>
      <h2>Few parts</h2>
      <p>A site is made of pages, a few small functions, an inbox for requests, and alerts with fixed wording. One person can maintain it.</p>
      <h2>After launch</h2>
      <p>We write down how everything works and where each account lives. From there you can run it yourself, or keep us on a monthly care plan.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ContactBlock />
</BaseLayout>
